---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import { absoluteUrl, isCommodityNode } from '../lib/site-variant';

if (!isCommodityNode) return Astro.redirect('/blog/');
const canonicalUrl = absoluteUrl('/privacy/');
---

<Base
  title="Privacy"
  metaTitle="CommodityNode Privacy"
  description="CommodityNode privacy and measurement principles."
  canonicalUrl={canonicalUrl}
>
  <article class="static-page prose">
    <p class="section-label">Trust</p>
    <h1>Privacy</h1>
    <p class="article-dek">
      CommodityNode works without an account, advertising identifier, or optional
      measurement. Necessary storage remembers only the privacy choice you make.
    </p>

    <h2>Data the site receives</h2>
    <p>
      Hosting and security providers may process ordinary request data such as IP
      address, user agent, requested path, time, and error details. These records
      support delivery, abuse prevention, and incident response. CommodityNode does
      not create an account or advertising profile from a public research visit.
    </p>

    <h2>Optional aggregate measurement</h2>
    <p>
      If you allow analytics, the browser may send a bounded event name, product
      surface, route type, and approved placement label. The event excludes email,
      name, account or session identifiers, free text, URL queries, and referrer.
      Events are stored only as daily aggregate counters and expire after 400 days.
      Declining analytics does not reduce access or functionality.
    </p>

    <h2>Advertising</h2>
    <p>
      Advertising is currently disabled site-wide. The advertising preference is a
      fail-closed control for future, manually reviewed inventory; choosing it does
      not load an ad today. CommodityNode will not enable advertising until the
      provider, retention terms, jurisdictional consent requirements, and eligible
      page list are documented and tested.
    </p>

    <h2>Your controls</h2>
    <p>
      You can reject optional storage on the first prompt or reopen
      <button type="button" class="inline-privacy-button" data-open-privacy-settings>
        privacy settings
      </button>
      at any time. A new consent-policy version invalidates the previous choice and
      asks again.
    </p>

    <h2>Contact and corrections</h2>
    <p>
      Privacy or source-attribution issues can be reported through the public repository. Do not include confidential information in a public issue.
    </p>
    <p>Policy version 1 · Effective July 28, 2026</p>
  </article>
</Base>
